orthant 2 release

@ 1 0 0 10172b47c55c58d0109781ea5d900299
+   entry #trees   every `Markup.Tree` in the message, wherever it is nested

@ 1 0 0 1639616f7496753a0e7bfbb34a978b50
+       row  `Tree(omitted, children)`  the tree which explains a failed contextual resolution; `omitted` counts the nodes left out for length
+       row  `Node(role, name, note, repeated, children)`  one node of such a tree: its `Role`, the `name` of what was sought, found or proposed, a `note` on it, and whether its subtree was shown earlier and is left out

@ 2 0 0 10bf172a4564103f045e0cb5dc62190c
+       The children of a `Tree` or a `Node` are its child `Node`s, interleaved with the
+       `Textual` line breaks and box-drawing which draw the same tree as plain text; `#nodes`
+       gives the `Node`s alone.
+

@ 0 2 0 1ca10bd465bb9b721b93a40f0570ae9a
+       decides the node: `type`, `sym`, `name`, `code` and `tree` have their own cases, as has
+       a `node` whose `role` is one of `.Role`'s, and any other kind is `Spanned`.

@ 1 0 0 0fc683c815a09c6a02b5b58070de4ac4
+   entry .wrap   wraps text in a marker of a kind, with attributes, as the compiler's own writer does
+       For a macro whose message should keep its structure: under `-Zsemantic-diagnostics` the
+       marker reaches `.parse` intact, and every other reader sees only the text inside it.
+   entry .Role   the part a `Node` plays in a tree: `Resolving`, `Candidate`, `Requires`, `Propose`, `Prohibits` or `Found`
+     entry #glyph   the symbol the role is drawn with
+     entry #word   the role's name in lower case, as the `role` attribute of a marker has it

@ 1 0 0 18576687bfc961a61f33a50051c88d6f
+   entry #nodes   the child `Node`s of a `Tree` or a `Node`, without the text which draws them
